1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:03,378
♪ Oh, Mamang Sastre…♪

2
00:00:03,461 --> 00:00:09,300
[♪"MAMANG SASTRE" PLAYING♪]

3
00:00:09,384 --> 00:00:10,802
♪ Oh, Mamang Sastre…♪

4
00:00:10,885 --> 00:00:12,762
♪ Hawak ang gunting… ♪

5
00:00:12,846 --> 00:00:14,556
♪ Isang hiwa ♪

6
00:00:14,639 --> 00:00:16,641
♪ Tapos ang usapin ♪

7
00:00:16,725 --> 00:00:20,270
Mercado is organizing an event,
and all the trackers will be there.

8
00:00:20,353 --> 00:00:23,648
Gather all
the information and we will strike,

9
00:00:23,732 --> 00:00:25,942
and they will never
know what is ahead of them.

10
00:00:26,025 --> 00:00:28,695
That's not the dress
code for our tea party.

11
00:00:28,778 --> 00:00:29,446
We have a party?

12
00:00:29,529 --> 00:00:30,905
You forgot?

13
00:00:30,989 --> 00:00:33,700
Looks like
you double-booked a party today, Love.

14
00:00:33,783 --> 00:00:36,411
Toast to our father…

15
00:00:36,494 --> 00:00:37,579
Ohh…

16
00:00:37,662 --> 00:00:40,331
To his happy retirement!

17
00:00:40,415 --> 00:00:41,666
- Yes.
- Retirement, indeed.

18
00:00:41,750 --> 00:00:42,625
- [clinks]
- [chuckles]

19
00:00:42,709 --> 00:00:45,128
- Let's take.
- Oh, ta-- take.

20
00:00:45,211 --> 00:00:46,212
Uhm, how are you there?

21
00:00:46,296 --> 00:00:49,299
I really don't feel good about this event.

22
00:00:49,382 --> 00:00:50,425
But I don't know why.

23
00:00:50,508 --> 00:00:53,136
Anyway, I'm on my way. I'll get ready.

24
00:00:53,219 --> 00:00:56,264
Everybody, prepare for phase two.

25
00:00:56,347 --> 00:00:57,140
Let's go!

26
00:01:00,018 --> 00:01:01,853
[metal screeching, then clangs]

27
00:01:01,936 --> 00:01:04,064
Where is the legendary Master Cutter?

28
00:01:04,147 --> 00:01:04,981
Is he here already?

29
00:01:05,065 --> 00:01:06,483
I would love to meet him.

30
00:01:06,566 --> 00:01:07,776
[darts whizzing & gunshots]

31
00:01:07,859 --> 00:01:09,903
- [screaming & panicking]
- [electricity crackles]

32
00:01:09,986 --> 00:01:11,071
[weapon swooshes, then clangs]

33
00:01:11,154 --> 00:01:12,447
[gunshots] [screaming & panicking]

34
00:01:12,530 --> 00:01:13,907
Let's wait for Sir Samir's signal first.

35
00:01:13,990 --> 00:01:16,493
[darts whizzing & gunshots]

36
00:01:16,576 --> 00:01:17,160
[music continues]

37
00:01:17,243 --> 00:01:17,744
[groans]

38
00:01:18,787 --> 00:01:19,996
[grunts & groans]

39
00:01:20,080 --> 00:01:21,122
[dagger swishes] [growls]

40
00:01:21,206 --> 00:01:22,040
[thuds] [groans]

41
00:01:22,123 --> 00:01:24,125
I know Samir is behind this.

42
00:01:24,209 --> 00:01:25,168
Gotcha.

43
00:01:25,251 --> 00:01:26,294
[explosion & rumbles]

44
00:01:26,377 --> 00:01:27,337
Do you have Mercado?

45
00:01:27,420 --> 00:01:28,880
We've removed the body already.

46
00:01:28,963 --> 00:01:30,173
Where is Atoy?

47
00:01:30,256 --> 00:01:31,466
We could've been taken out.

48
00:01:31,549 --> 00:01:32,175
So, we must leave!

49
00:01:32,258 --> 00:01:33,092
Uno?

50
00:01:33,176 --> 00:01:34,260
What happened here?

51
00:01:34,344 --> 00:01:35,595
Sir Mercado--

52
00:01:35,678 --> 00:01:37,055
I'll come back for you.

53
00:01:38,223 --> 00:01:41,142
[music continues]

54
00:01:51,277 --> 00:01:51,986
[clatters]

55
00:01:52,070 --> 00:01:57,325
[music intensifies]

56
00:01:58,701 --> 00:02:00,662
Belladonna. [mouthing words]

57
00:02:02,497 --> 00:02:03,164
[music fades]

58
00:02:04,833 --> 00:02:05,583
[thudding]

59
00:02:18,680 --> 00:02:25,645
[suspicious music playing]

60
00:02:26,354 --> 00:02:27,480
[knocks]

61
00:02:29,274 --> 00:02:30,316
[music fades]

62
00:02:31,568 --> 00:02:38,241
[tense music playing]

63
00:02:44,706 --> 00:02:46,040
Brother, Brother, he's still alive!

64
00:02:46,124 --> 00:02:47,125
Let's get him, let's get him.

65
00:02:47,208 --> 00:02:48,960
- And-- under the table!
- Uno.

66
00:02:49,043 --> 00:02:50,503
- Where?
- The woman is still moving!

67
00:02:50,587 --> 00:02:52,005
Hold him.

68
00:02:52,088 --> 00:02:53,172
Okay, I'll take care of it.

69
00:02:53,256 --> 00:02:57,510
[music swells]

70
00:03:03,516 --> 00:03:04,017
Jesabel?

71
00:03:07,812 --> 00:03:08,563
[music fades]

72
00:03:08,646 --> 00:03:09,772
[foreboding music playing]

73
00:03:09,856 --> 00:03:12,358
[bomb ticking]

74
00:03:12,442 --> 00:03:14,110
We need to get out
of here, there's a bomb!

75
00:03:14,193 --> 00:03:16,112
Come on, hurry.

76
00:03:16,195 --> 00:03:17,030
[music intensifies]

77
00:03:17,113 --> 00:03:19,532
[bomb ticking]

78
00:03:25,955 --> 00:03:27,749
[explosions]

79
00:03:27,832 --> 00:03:30,168
[music swells]

80
00:03:30,251 --> 00:03:33,504
[rousing music playing]

81
00:03:40,220 --> 00:03:42,555
[theme music playing]

82
00:03:42,639 --> 00:03:44,974
♪ Oh, Mister Tailor… ♪

83
00:03:45,058 --> 00:03:50,980
["Mamang Sastre" playing]

84
00:03:51,064 --> 00:03:53,191
♪ Wait a moment, Mister Tailor ♪

85
00:03:53,274 --> 00:03:54,525
♪ Can you be the one to sew ♪

86
00:03:54,609 --> 00:04:00,156
♪ My polo's hole that fits just under
the armpit ♪ ♪ In every cut of cloth ♪

87
00:04:00,240 --> 00:04:02,492
♪ There's a secret behind it ♪

88
00:04:02,575 --> 00:04:04,410
♪ If your measurement is wrong,

89
00:04:04,494 --> 00:04:08,957
the whole fit turns crooked ♪

90
00:04:09,040 --> 00:04:09,666
[gunshots]

91
00:04:09,749 --> 00:04:11,417
♪ Oh, Mister Tailor ♪

92
00:04:11,501 --> 00:04:13,628
♪ Holding the scissors ♪

93
00:04:13,711 --> 00:04:15,380
[music swells]

94
00:04:15,463 --> 00:04:17,298
(Fix this)

95
00:04:17,882 --> 00:04:18,716
[music fades]

96
00:04:20,969 --> 00:04:27,934
[sirens wailing]

97
00:04:30,436 --> 00:04:33,481
Sir, only a few people go in

98
00:04:33,564 --> 00:04:35,066
and out of that shop.

99
00:04:35,149 --> 00:04:36,776
I was wondering,

100
00:04:37,485 --> 00:04:40,655
because it doesn't usually have customers.

101
00:04:40,738 --> 00:04:43,866
But earlier, there were so many people.

102
00:04:43,950 --> 00:04:45,994
Maybe more than twenty.

103
00:04:46,577 --> 00:04:48,913
And they looked wealthy.

104
00:04:48,997 --> 00:04:50,456
More than twenty?

105
00:04:50,540 --> 00:04:51,291
Yes!

106
00:04:51,374 --> 00:04:54,168
What time did this happen?

107
00:04:54,252 --> 00:04:55,295
Around…

108
00:04:55,378 --> 00:04:57,463
maybe six or eight o'clock.

109
00:04:57,547 --> 00:04:58,756
There were so many people,

110
00:04:58,840 --> 00:05:01,801
and they were noisy.
They disturbed my sleep.

111
00:05:01,884 --> 00:05:04,846
I was supposed to buy goods tomorrow.

112
00:05:04,929 --> 00:05:05,722
It was annoying.

113
00:05:05,805 --> 00:05:11,394
But, Sir, someone arrived. A handsome man!

114
00:05:11,477 --> 00:05:14,188
But he was locked out.

115
00:05:14,272 --> 00:05:17,317
So, what he did was go around.

116
00:05:17,400 --> 00:05:19,569
Then, I heard…

117
00:05:19,652 --> 00:05:21,612
Ah, like gunfire.

118
00:05:21,696 --> 00:05:23,406
There was even an explosion.

119
00:05:23,489 --> 00:05:25,825
Then, I saw the handsome guy.

120
00:05:25,908 --> 00:05:28,077
He came back to the front.

121
00:05:28,161 --> 00:05:29,620
He removed the lock.

122
00:05:29,704 --> 00:05:31,581
Then, he went inside.

123
00:05:31,664 --> 00:05:33,416
Ah, I went in too,

124
00:05:33,499 --> 00:05:35,335
because I wanted to
know what was happening.

125
00:05:35,918 --> 00:05:38,921
Then, we brought out two wounded people.

126
00:05:39,005 --> 00:05:40,548
Then suddenly, boom!

127
00:05:41,382 --> 00:05:42,341
It exploded!

128
00:05:42,425 --> 00:05:44,052
There was a bomb!

129
00:05:44,135 --> 00:05:46,095
We were thrown off; my body hurts.

130
00:05:46,637 --> 00:05:47,680
I thought

131
00:05:48,681 --> 00:05:50,725
I was going to die because…

132
00:05:50,808 --> 00:05:52,101
I haven't gotten married yet.

133
00:05:52,185 --> 00:05:54,437
[sneaky music playing]

134
00:05:54,520 --> 00:05:55,480
Uhm…

135
00:05:56,230 --> 00:05:59,025
Where's the man you mentioned?

136
00:05:59,108 --> 00:06:02,487
Ah, we brought the wounded

137
00:06:02,570 --> 00:06:03,821
to his vehicle.

138
00:06:03,905 --> 00:06:07,033
Then, he took them to the hospital.

139
00:06:07,116 --> 00:06:09,827
But the police didn't catch up to him.

140
00:06:09,911 --> 00:06:11,287
But, Sir,

141
00:06:11,829 --> 00:06:13,748
just between us.

142
00:06:14,332 --> 00:06:15,958
It seemed like he didn't
want the police to find him.

143
00:06:17,794 --> 00:06:18,961
Why do you say that?

144
00:06:19,045 --> 00:06:21,297
Because when I said

145
00:06:21,380 --> 00:06:23,049
I'd call the police,

146
00:06:23,132 --> 00:06:24,175
he stopped me.

147
00:06:24,258 --> 00:06:25,968
I wonder why?

148
00:06:26,052 --> 00:06:27,345
Why didn't you ask?

149
00:06:27,428 --> 00:06:28,846
Well, we're not close.

150
00:06:28,930 --> 00:06:30,473
If we were close, I'd ask.

151
00:06:30,556 --> 00:06:32,016
That's true.

152
00:06:33,142 --> 00:06:34,435
Uhm…

153
00:06:34,519 --> 00:06:35,770
Ah, okay.

154
00:06:35,853 --> 00:06:38,314
You really don't know
which hospital they were taken to?

155
00:06:38,397 --> 00:06:41,109
And did you get the man's name?

156
00:06:41,192 --> 00:06:42,443
No, I didn't.

157
00:06:42,527 --> 00:06:46,155
I also didn't get his plate number.

158
00:06:46,239 --> 00:06:47,448
[playful music playing]

159
00:06:47,532 --> 00:06:49,450
Eh-- do you have food there?

160
00:06:49,534 --> 00:06:51,619
I'm hungry, you're
asking too many questions.

161
00:06:51,702 --> 00:06:52,662
I don't have food,

162
00:06:52,745 --> 00:06:54,288
but I have a gun.

163
00:06:54,372 --> 00:06:55,456
No, I'm full after all.

164
00:06:55,540 --> 00:06:56,332
It's fine, Sir.

165
00:06:56,415 --> 00:06:57,208
- Are you okay?
- I'm okay.

166
00:06:57,291 --> 00:06:57,875
All right, go back there.

167
00:06:58,626 --> 00:06:59,544
- Okay, Sir.
- Yes.

168
00:06:59,627 --> 00:07:02,505
[music continues]

169
00:07:02,588 --> 00:07:05,299
[ambulance siren wailing in the distance]

170
00:07:05,383 --> 00:07:06,259
Thank you, Doc.

171
00:07:12,348 --> 00:07:15,893
[muffled chattering in the distance]

172
00:07:15,977 --> 00:07:18,312
Si-- si-- Sir Atoy…

173
00:07:19,272 --> 00:07:21,399
Am-- am I still alive?

174
00:07:21,482 --> 00:07:23,192
You're in the ER.

175
00:07:23,776 --> 00:07:24,819
I brought you here.

176
00:07:26,070 --> 00:07:27,613
Your CT scan is cleared.

177
00:07:28,489 --> 00:07:29,615
I didn't want to bring you here,

178
00:07:29,699 --> 00:07:30,575
but it was necessary.

179
00:07:30,658 --> 00:07:33,536
We needed to examine
your head, in case of internal bleeding.

180
00:07:33,619 --> 00:07:34,370
But are you okay?

181
00:07:35,872 --> 00:07:36,497
Mmm.

182
00:07:36,581 --> 00:07:38,791
Yes. Th-- thank you, Sir Atoy.

183
00:07:39,792 --> 00:07:41,210
What about Sir Mercado?

184
00:07:42,044 --> 00:07:43,880
[muffled chattering in the distance]

185
00:07:43,963 --> 00:07:45,131
He wasn't backstage.

186
00:07:45,965 --> 00:07:47,717
Uno is in the ICU.

187
00:07:48,634 --> 00:07:50,344
Looks like it's just
the two of us survived.

188
00:07:52,680 --> 00:07:55,057
Do you have any idea
where they took the trackers?

189
00:07:55,141 --> 00:07:57,185
Huh? Where did they go?

190
00:07:57,268 --> 00:07:58,811
What about Sir Mercado,
what did they do to him?

191
00:07:59,604 --> 00:08:01,230
Was Samir behind this?

192
00:08:01,314 --> 00:08:03,441
Do you know why this happened?

193
00:08:04,358 --> 00:08:06,402
Did Samir take all of them?

194
00:08:07,236 --> 00:08:09,906
Eh, I really don't know.

195
00:08:10,531 --> 00:08:13,910
The last thing Sir Mercado told me

196
00:08:13,993 --> 00:08:16,037
was that he had a big mission to announce

197
00:08:16,120 --> 00:08:19,457
about Belladonna and Obsidian.

198
00:08:19,540 --> 00:08:22,335
Do you know anything about that?

199
00:08:22,418 --> 00:08:23,836
Belladonna.

200
00:08:23,920 --> 00:08:27,757
[suspicious music playing]

201
00:08:29,175 --> 00:08:31,052
I saw this backstage.

202
00:08:31,135 --> 00:08:31,677
[music fades]

203
00:08:31,761 --> 00:08:32,678
It looks like it was written by…

204
00:08:34,055 --> 00:08:35,264
Colonel Mercado.

205
00:08:36,641 --> 00:08:40,353
Sir Atoy, M-00,
this is Sir Mercado's profile number.

206
00:08:41,854 --> 00:08:44,148
Sir Atoy, let's call the police.

207
00:08:44,232 --> 00:08:46,734
Let's ask for their help to catch Samir.

208
00:08:46,817 --> 00:08:48,319
We can't, we can't contact

209
00:08:48,402 --> 00:08:49,237
the police.

210
00:08:49,320 --> 00:08:49,987
Huh?

211
00:08:50,780 --> 00:08:52,240
That's not in our protocol,

212
00:08:52,323 --> 00:08:53,074
you should know that.

213
00:08:54,283 --> 00:08:56,452
Ye-- yes, Sir Atoy.

214
00:08:56,536 --> 00:09:00,248
It's in Chapter 3 on Police Intervention.

215
00:09:00,331 --> 00:09:02,041
In cases of deaths and accidents,

216
00:09:02,124 --> 00:09:05,795
within the agency's
premises or official gatherings,

217
00:09:05,878 --> 00:09:08,339
the police must not be informed,

218
00:09:08,422 --> 00:09:10,800
in order to protect the agency

219
00:09:10,883 --> 00:09:12,885
and safeguard the privacy

220
00:09:12,969 --> 00:09:15,429
of The Agency's clients and trackers.

221
00:09:15,513 --> 00:09:16,556
Okay, good.

222
00:09:17,306 --> 00:09:18,891
Your mind is still sharp.

223
00:09:19,767 --> 00:09:21,352
I'll have you discharged,

224
00:09:21,435 --> 00:09:22,853
so we can leave.

225
00:09:23,479 --> 00:09:25,565
[rousing music playing]

226
00:09:27,817 --> 00:09:28,859
Yes. They already moved.

227
00:09:28,943 --> 00:09:30,570
The dialysis area is over there.

228
00:09:30,653 --> 00:09:31,237
I saw it. Okay, thank you.

229
00:09:31,320 --> 00:09:32,238
All right. Thank you.

230
00:09:36,117 --> 00:09:37,702
Ah, excuse me.

231
00:09:38,786 --> 00:09:41,998
The dialysis area is
over there. Just go straight.

232
00:09:42,081 --> 00:09:43,207
[pleasant music playing]

233
00:09:43,291 --> 00:09:44,208
Wait, wait.

234
00:09:44,292 --> 00:09:46,419
Why? Do I look like I have kidney disease?

235
00:09:46,502 --> 00:09:47,753
[music continues]

236
00:09:47,837 --> 00:09:49,505
No, Sir.

237
00:09:49,589 --> 00:09:50,506
Sorry, it's just--

238
00:09:50,590 --> 00:09:53,467
that's what people in line usually ask me.

239
00:09:53,551 --> 00:09:55,845
Ah-- the dialysis center moved there,

240
00:09:55,928 --> 00:09:56,679
just in case.

241
00:09:56,762 --> 00:09:58,889
I don't care about the dialysis center.

242
00:10:00,099 --> 00:10:02,226
You're the guy who was at Gregorio

243
00:10:02,310 --> 00:10:04,145
when the explosion happened, right?

244
00:10:04,228 --> 00:10:07,106
Because the description matches.

245
00:10:07,189 --> 00:10:09,150
Your height, your looks.

246
00:10:09,233 --> 00:10:11,360
You look like Marimar's husband.

247
00:10:11,444 --> 00:10:13,321
Oh, don't-- oh, and…

248
00:10:13,404 --> 00:10:14,113
[sniffs]

249
00:10:14,196 --> 00:10:15,448
You smell like something. [smirks]

250
00:10:15,531 --> 00:10:16,532
You smell like grilled food.

251
00:10:16,616 --> 00:10:18,576
[tense music playing]

252
00:10:18,659 --> 00:10:19,410
Oh, right?

253
00:10:19,493 --> 00:10:20,453
Don't deny it.

254
00:10:20,536 --> 00:10:21,329
I'm a policeman.

255
00:10:21,412 --> 00:10:25,750
Senior investigator Elias Matangbaka.

256
00:10:25,833 --> 00:10:27,084
- Right?
- Right, Sir.

257
00:10:27,168 --> 00:10:29,629
Ah, what do you need?

258
00:10:29,712 --> 00:10:31,213
What happened there?

259
00:10:31,297 --> 00:10:36,802
I was told more than
twenty people went inside.

260
00:10:36,886 --> 00:10:38,387
But when the explosion happened,

261
00:10:38,471 --> 00:10:40,431
the people disappeared.

262
00:10:40,514 --> 00:10:41,557
What happened there?

263
00:10:41,641 --> 00:10:44,560
Ah, well, Sir. I really don't know.

264
00:10:44,644 --> 00:10:47,897
Actually, it was my boss's birthday.

265
00:10:47,980 --> 00:10:49,148
I didn't make it in time.

266
00:10:49,231 --> 00:10:50,691
I don't know what happened, Sir.

267
00:10:50,775 --> 00:10:52,485
I just helped.

268
00:10:52,568 --> 00:10:53,861
That's why I'm here.

269
00:10:54,862 --> 00:10:57,239
You know, what
you're saying isn't convincing.

270
00:10:57,323 --> 00:10:59,659
Better come with me to the precinct,

271
00:10:59,742 --> 00:11:00,951
I'll question you there.

272
00:11:01,035 --> 00:11:02,078
Ah, sorry.

273
00:11:02,161 --> 00:11:03,788
I won't go with you.

274
00:11:03,871 --> 00:11:06,499
Because I know under the law,

275
00:11:06,582 --> 00:11:08,250
if there's no subpoena

276
00:11:08,334 --> 00:11:11,712
or warrant of arrest,
I don't have to go with you.

277
00:11:11,796 --> 00:11:12,338
Sorry.

278
00:11:13,005 --> 00:11:14,673
Yes. I was just testing you.

279
00:11:14,757 --> 00:11:19,011
[sneaky music playing]

280
00:11:19,095 --> 00:11:24,392
You're the only
conscious survivor from the explosion.

281
00:11:25,017 --> 00:11:27,436
Uhm, can you tell me

282
00:11:27,520 --> 00:11:29,063
what you saw

283
00:11:29,146 --> 00:11:32,733
from the time you arrived
until the explosion happened?

284
00:11:32,817 --> 00:11:33,859
Uhm…

285
00:11:35,027 --> 00:11:36,278
[mysterious music playing]

286
00:11:36,362 --> 00:11:37,571
Explosion?

287
00:11:38,322 --> 00:11:39,657
When did that happen?

288
00:11:41,158 --> 00:11:43,327
Ah-- yes. There was an explosion.

289
00:11:43,828 --> 00:11:44,954
You don't remember?

290
00:11:45,037 --> 00:11:45,913
Ah, Sir.

291
00:11:46,789 --> 00:11:47,915
Oh no, maybe…

292
00:11:47,998 --> 00:11:50,626
Maybe he doesn't remember anymore.

293
00:11:50,709 --> 00:11:52,586
Maybe his brain was affected

294
00:11:52,670 --> 00:11:54,046
by the explosion.

295
00:11:54,130 --> 00:11:55,881
Like amnesia, Sir.

296
00:11:55,965 --> 00:11:56,799
That's what I feel.

297
00:11:58,551 --> 00:11:59,718
Are you his doctor?

298
00:12:01,262 --> 00:12:02,054
Huh?

299
00:12:02,138 --> 00:12:05,349
Or do you just watch those TV series?

300
00:12:05,433 --> 00:12:08,894
Ah-- And you're the only one
who brought him here, helped him.

301
00:12:08,978 --> 00:12:10,604
Do you know each other?

302
00:12:10,688 --> 00:12:12,189
Ah, Sir, sorry.

303
00:12:12,273 --> 00:12:14,233
No, I just offered help.

304
00:12:14,900 --> 00:12:15,443
Ah, I'll leave now.

305
00:12:15,526 --> 00:12:18,571
♪ I have a balloon ♪

306
00:12:18,654 --> 00:12:21,991
♪ It flew into the sky ♪

307
00:12:22,074 --> 00:12:24,452
♪ I didn't see it anymore,

308
00:12:24,535 --> 00:12:27,163
It had already popped ♪

309
00:12:27,246 --> 00:12:28,873
Brother, buy me a balloon.

310
00:12:28,956 --> 00:12:32,418
I want a balloon, because it-- it popped.

311
00:12:33,127 --> 00:12:34,545
Brother, buy me a balloon--

312
00:12:34,628 --> 00:12:35,713
This doesn't look like amnesia.

313
00:12:35,796 --> 00:12:36,922
Looks more like mental illness.

314
00:12:37,756 --> 00:12:40,092
Ah-- ah, okay, okay.

315
00:12:40,176 --> 00:12:42,428
Uhm, just rest for now.

316
00:12:42,511 --> 00:12:43,971
Will you buy me a balloon?

317
00:12:44,054 --> 00:12:44,805
Yes, I'll buy you one.

318
00:12:44,889 --> 00:12:46,765
Two, okay? I want two.

319
00:12:46,849 --> 00:12:49,852
- Yes.
- Because my balloon popped.

320
00:12:49,935 --> 00:12:51,395
[playful music playing]

321
00:12:51,479 --> 00:12:53,647
All right. I'll come back later.

322
00:12:54,231 --> 00:12:55,316
Okay, Sir, ah--

323
00:12:55,399 --> 00:12:56,650
Two balloons, okay.

324
00:12:56,734 --> 00:12:58,402
I'll leave now, Sir.

325
00:12:58,486 --> 00:13:01,197
[rousing music playing]

326
00:13:04,992 --> 00:13:05,868
You were good.

327
00:13:06,660 --> 00:13:08,204
I thought you'd really gone crazy.

328
00:13:08,287 --> 00:13:09,914
[suspicious music playing]

329
00:13:09,997 --> 00:13:10,623
All right.

330
00:13:11,290 --> 00:13:13,876
But we really need to get out of here now.

331
00:13:13,959 --> 00:13:16,420
[music swells]

332
00:13:16,504 --> 00:13:19,757
Sir Atoy, I'm really scared.

333
00:13:21,592 --> 00:13:24,720
I'm afraid they'll come back for me.

334
00:13:24,803 --> 00:13:26,680
That they'll kill me.

335
00:13:26,764 --> 00:13:28,974
I'm scared, Sir Atoy.

336
00:13:29,058 --> 00:13:29,558
[music continues]

337
00:13:31,060 --> 00:13:32,228
I'll take care of you.

338
00:13:33,062 --> 00:13:33,646
We'll get out of here.

339
00:13:39,318 --> 00:13:39,818
[music fades]

340
00:13:39,902 --> 00:13:41,737
An explosion occurred

341
00:13:41,820 --> 00:13:44,907
a few hours ago here in Barangay Gregorio.

342
00:13:44,990 --> 00:13:48,494
Former Colonel Levi Mercado,
a former army general,

343
00:13:48,577 --> 00:13:50,788
who was celebrating his birthday party

344
00:13:50,871 --> 00:13:52,331
at the establishment,

345
00:13:52,414 --> 00:13:53,832
is currently missing.

346
00:13:53,916 --> 00:13:57,211
Meanwhile, one of the guests,

347
00:13:57,294 --> 00:13:58,963
identified as Uno Alcaraz,

348
00:13:59,046 --> 00:14:01,131
is in the hospital in critical condition.

349
00:14:01,215 --> 00:14:05,177
There are also several bodies still
unidentified by authorities.

350
00:14:05,886 --> 00:14:09,181
[pensive music playing]

351
00:14:09,265 --> 00:14:11,934
Where could Sir Mercado be?

352
00:14:12,017 --> 00:14:13,185
How is he now?

353
00:14:13,811 --> 00:14:16,230
Maybe the Obsidian already killed him.

354
00:14:16,313 --> 00:14:17,856
[music continues]

355
00:14:17,940 --> 00:14:20,150
Sir Atoy, I'm really worried

356
00:14:20,234 --> 00:14:22,403
about Sir Mercado,
because he's like a father to me.

357
00:14:23,404 --> 00:14:24,572
Not just you.

358
00:14:24,655 --> 00:14:26,073
[music continues]

359
00:14:26,156 --> 00:14:30,035
Colonel Mercado is also
an important part of my life.

360
00:14:30,119 --> 00:14:32,204
[music continues]

361
00:14:32,288 --> 00:14:33,330
From now on, we won't say anything

362
00:14:33,414 --> 00:14:34,540
to the police.

363
00:14:36,375 --> 00:14:37,710
We need to be consistent

364
00:14:37,793 --> 00:14:39,378
with what we told them earlier.

365
00:14:39,461 --> 00:14:40,921
[music continues]

366
00:14:41,005 --> 00:14:42,756
Just wait for me here.

367
00:14:43,674 --> 00:14:44,758
I'll get something.

368
00:14:44,842 --> 00:14:46,802
[music continues]

369
00:14:46,886 --> 00:14:47,469
[car door shuts]

370
00:14:47,553 --> 00:14:49,680
[music swells]

371
00:15:01,525 --> 00:15:02,318
[music fades]

372
00:15:03,027 --> 00:15:04,028
Love…

373
00:15:07,031 --> 00:15:08,616
I'm so sorry.

374
00:15:08,699 --> 00:15:11,118
[somber music playing]

375
00:15:11,869 --> 00:15:17,041
We just were just talking
about your boss earlier, and now…

376
00:15:18,709 --> 00:15:20,210
he's missing,

377
00:15:22,129 --> 00:15:24,632
and your companions are missing too.

378
00:15:24,715 --> 00:15:27,968
[music continues]

379
00:15:28,969 --> 00:15:33,015
What about Uno, how is he?

380
00:15:34,850 --> 00:15:36,602
He's in the ICU.

381
00:15:37,311 --> 00:15:39,355
[music continues]

382
00:15:39,438 --> 00:15:40,773
Love…

383
00:15:40,856 --> 00:15:42,399
[music continues]

384
00:15:42,483 --> 00:15:46,904
If you had arrived at the party on time…

385
00:15:46,987 --> 00:15:49,740
[music continues]

386
00:15:49,823 --> 00:15:52,368
- Maybe--
- Maybe I wouldn't be here now.

387
00:15:53,953 --> 00:15:56,205
Our family's night would be different.

388
00:15:56,789 --> 00:16:01,627
[pensive music playing]

389
00:16:03,587 --> 00:16:05,506
I can't imagine

390
00:16:05,589 --> 00:16:07,883
how hard this is for you.

391
00:16:07,967 --> 00:16:10,010
[music continues]

392
00:16:10,636 --> 00:16:12,429
But I'm so grateful

393
00:16:13,389 --> 00:16:16,058
you left your old life behind, Love.

394
00:16:16,141 --> 00:16:17,726
[music continues]

395
00:16:17,810 --> 00:16:19,937
That you're retired now.

396
00:16:20,020 --> 00:16:23,691
[music continues]

397
00:16:30,656 --> 00:16:32,491
I wouldn't have been late to that party,

398
00:16:32,574 --> 00:16:35,619
if our kids hadn't played with me.

399
00:16:35,703 --> 00:16:38,872
[music continues]

400
00:16:39,373 --> 00:16:41,166
They had no idea…

401
00:16:42,793 --> 00:16:44,378
that they saved my life.

402
00:16:45,087 --> 00:16:48,257
[music continues]

403
00:16:48,340 --> 00:16:50,634
That's why we're still complete today.

404
00:16:56,890 --> 00:17:03,397
♪ sentimental music playing ♪

405
00:17:22,207 --> 00:17:23,459
[pensive music playing]

406
00:17:23,542 --> 00:17:26,170
Sorry you had to wait so long in the car.

407
00:17:26,253 --> 00:17:28,589
I had to put the kids to sleep,

408
00:17:29,214 --> 00:17:31,175
and I brought your things.

409
00:17:32,217 --> 00:17:33,218
[grunts]

410
00:17:33,302 --> 00:17:34,428
Take it easy.

411
00:17:34,511 --> 00:17:35,846
[music continues]

412
00:17:35,929 --> 00:17:36,972
Here we are.

413
00:17:38,015 --> 00:17:40,601
[door hinge squeaks]

414
00:17:40,684 --> 00:17:41,185
[light switch clicks]

415
00:17:41,268 --> 00:17:44,480
[music continues]

416
00:17:47,816 --> 00:17:50,444
This used to be my kids' room.

417
00:17:51,403 --> 00:17:52,613
Ah, under renovation.

418
00:17:52,696 --> 00:17:55,032
Sorry if it smells like paint.

419
00:17:55,657 --> 00:17:57,284
You can rest here for now.

420
00:17:58,619 --> 00:18:00,204
In the morning, I'll be here.

421
00:18:00,287 --> 00:18:01,789
I work at the tailoring shop.

422
00:18:01,872 --> 00:18:04,708
Me, Godmother Cita, and Ame.

423
00:18:05,667 --> 00:18:07,086
- Okay? Don't worry.
- Thank you.

424
00:18:09,379 --> 00:18:12,883
Sorry, I have to hide you here first.

425
00:18:12,966 --> 00:18:15,177
I told my family I'm retired.

426
00:18:15,260 --> 00:18:17,721
[music continues]

427
00:18:17,805 --> 00:18:19,223
[clicks tongue] Get some rest.

428
00:18:20,474 --> 00:18:21,934
Thank you, Sir Atoy.

429
00:18:22,017 --> 00:18:28,982
[suspicious music playing]

430
00:18:44,248 --> 00:18:45,082
[music fades]

431
00:18:45,165 --> 00:18:47,668
- We did a good job today!
- Cheers! Cheers, cheers!

432
00:18:47,751 --> 00:18:49,419
[clinking] Whoo!

433
00:18:50,712 --> 00:18:51,505
[door closes]

434
00:18:52,464 --> 00:18:53,215
Samir!

435
00:18:54,341 --> 00:18:55,259
Are you okay?

436
00:18:55,342 --> 00:18:56,593
Relax.

437
00:18:57,344 --> 00:18:58,720
Join us!

438
00:18:58,804 --> 00:18:59,596
[table thuds]

439
00:19:00,514 --> 00:19:02,850
[somber music playing]

440
00:19:02,933 --> 00:19:03,934
Are you good?

441
00:19:05,018 --> 00:19:06,937
[ominous music playing]

442
00:19:07,020 --> 00:19:09,273
You want me to relax, hmm?

443
00:19:10,107 --> 00:19:12,276
You want me to have a good time, yeah?

444
00:19:13,819 --> 00:19:15,654
[sighs]

445
00:19:15,737 --> 00:19:18,031
Mercado is missing.

446
00:19:18,866 --> 00:19:21,493
He's the only man
who can recognize Belladonna

447
00:19:21,577 --> 00:19:23,078
and he's gone.

448
00:19:23,662 --> 00:19:24,705
If he escaped,

449
00:19:25,706 --> 00:19:27,374
he won't survive.

450
00:19:27,457 --> 00:19:28,959
He has fatal wounds.

451
00:19:29,042 --> 00:19:32,254
[music continues]

452
00:19:32,754 --> 00:19:35,716
Okay. For you, let's say, maybe he's dead.

453
00:19:36,341 --> 00:19:38,635
But Belladonna is still out there

454
00:19:38,719 --> 00:19:41,805
and she knows
the big plan. [music continues]

455
00:19:41,889 --> 00:19:44,683
If she talks about the Big Bang plot,

456
00:19:44,766 --> 00:19:47,561
we have a big problem!

457
00:19:48,145 --> 00:19:50,105
Big problem!

458
00:19:50,189 --> 00:19:52,232
[suspicious music playing]

459
00:19:53,859 --> 00:19:54,902
Boys, out.

460
00:19:55,402 --> 00:20:01,158
[music continues]

461
00:20:01,241 --> 00:20:02,326
Samir…

462
00:20:02,409 --> 00:20:03,827
[music continues]

463
00:20:03,911 --> 00:20:06,455
We have every one of Mercado's trackers.

464
00:20:07,164 --> 00:20:08,540
The very people he could have passed

465
00:20:08,624 --> 00:20:10,125
our plans to.

466
00:20:10,959 --> 00:20:12,794
But there's this one guy

467
00:20:12,878 --> 00:20:14,004
in the hospital and…

468
00:20:14,504 --> 00:20:16,924
maybe he could be dead in a few more days.

469
00:20:17,007 --> 00:20:21,470
[music continues]

470
00:20:23,138 --> 00:20:30,103
[phone ringing]

471
00:20:30,187 --> 00:20:32,940
[music continues]

472
00:20:33,023 --> 00:20:34,191
How's the inspection?

473
00:20:34,274 --> 00:20:41,198
[music continues]

474
00:20:42,282 --> 00:20:43,283
Okay, okay.

475
00:20:43,367 --> 00:20:46,828
[music swells]

476
00:20:46,912 --> 00:20:49,206
We have all the 28 trackers

477
00:20:49,289 --> 00:20:51,041
on their way to the warehouse.

478
00:20:51,124 --> 00:20:53,085
[music continues]

479
00:20:56,546 --> 00:20:57,547
28?

480
00:20:57,631 --> 00:20:59,591
Wait. We have a problem.

481
00:21:00,884 --> 00:21:03,512
30 trackers on manifest.

482
00:21:04,137 --> 00:21:06,306
One in the hospital, Uno Alcaraz.

483
00:21:06,390 --> 00:21:07,099
That's 29.

484
00:21:07,182 --> 00:21:10,018
That means we're missing somebody.

485
00:21:10,102 --> 00:21:10,894
[music continues]

486
00:21:10,978 --> 00:21:12,396
One tracker is still alive.

487
00:21:13,689 --> 00:21:14,773
That's impossible.

488
00:21:15,190 --> 00:21:17,234
I mean, no one escaped!

489
00:21:19,194 --> 00:21:21,655
[suspicious music playing]

490
00:21:21,738 --> 00:21:25,075
Maybe he did not arrive at the party.

491
00:21:25,701 --> 00:21:27,369
Maybe they were late.

492
00:21:27,452 --> 00:21:29,413
[music continues]

493
00:21:29,496 --> 00:21:32,833
Have you located
the body of Anthony Padua?

494
00:21:32,916 --> 00:21:35,294
I did not see him at the party.

495
00:21:35,919 --> 00:21:38,588
Our men have not
identified the bodies yet.

496
00:21:39,214 --> 00:21:42,134
I will update you once it has been done.

497
00:21:42,217 --> 00:21:43,260
[music continues]

498
00:21:43,885 --> 00:21:45,721
I have a bad feeling,

499
00:21:45,804 --> 00:21:49,266
Anthony Padua is still out there.

500
00:21:49,349 --> 00:21:51,768
[music continues]

501
00:21:59,484 --> 00:22:00,569
One.

502
00:22:03,155 --> 00:22:04,281
[clinks]

503
00:22:05,991 --> 00:22:07,868
Bro, you've been eating all the candy.

504
00:22:07,951 --> 00:22:09,619
These are for the clients.

505
00:22:10,162 --> 00:22:11,705
There aren't any yet!

506
00:22:11,788 --> 00:22:13,123
Then I'll just replace it.

507
00:22:14,708 --> 00:22:15,500
Come on.

508
00:22:15,584 --> 00:22:18,503
That's the only thing we can offer them--

509
00:22:19,588 --> 00:22:20,922
[pensive music playing]

510
00:22:21,590 --> 00:22:23,050
Bro.

511
00:22:23,133 --> 00:22:24,801
- Oh?
- What's this?

512
00:22:25,594 --> 00:22:26,094
Why?

513
00:22:27,012 --> 00:22:27,512
What's this?

514
00:22:27,596 --> 00:22:28,221
Why is there a gun here?

515
00:22:28,305 --> 00:22:29,264
Together with the staplers?

516
00:22:29,347 --> 00:22:31,600
- That's my gun. It's licensed.
- So what?

517
00:22:31,683 --> 00:22:33,894
Then it should be hidden in the safe.

518
00:22:33,977 --> 00:22:35,020
Put it there.

519
00:22:35,103 --> 00:22:37,939
Of course-- sometimes
Ibyang walks around here,

520
00:22:38,023 --> 00:22:38,815
she visits.

521
00:22:38,899 --> 00:22:40,525
Sometimes she rummages, borrows staplers.

522
00:22:40,609 --> 00:22:42,527
What if she opens it?
Then she'll see it, we'll be in trouble.

523
00:22:42,611 --> 00:22:43,737
[music continues]

524
00:22:43,820 --> 00:22:46,823
Bro, we should be responsible gun owners.

525
00:22:46,907 --> 00:22:48,200
Yes, it's risky.

526
00:22:48,283 --> 00:22:51,453
Remember that news before?

527
00:22:51,536 --> 00:22:55,165
Kids smuggled a gun into school.

528
00:22:55,248 --> 00:22:56,750
They wouldn't have gotten the gun

529
00:22:56,833 --> 00:22:59,169
if people around them had been careful.

530
00:22:59,252 --> 00:23:00,253
You're right.

531
00:23:00,337 --> 00:23:01,880
Sorry, sorry. I'll hide it now,

532
00:23:01,963 --> 00:23:03,340
- I'll hide it.
- Yes, let's put it there.

533
00:23:03,423 --> 00:23:05,383
[music swells]

534
00:23:05,467 --> 00:23:06,968
- Paldo!
- Someone might get hurt--

535
00:23:07,052 --> 00:23:08,553
- Emerson, look.
- Sir Nestor.

536
00:23:08,637 --> 00:23:09,679
Look at that.

537
00:23:10,305 --> 00:23:11,306
- Why?
- There was an explosion

538
00:23:11,389 --> 00:23:13,183
in Barangay Gregorio, it jolted.

539
00:23:13,266 --> 00:23:14,768
- Uno was badly hit.
- What?

540
00:23:14,851 --> 00:23:17,729
- Uno?
- Yes, and the ex-general,

541
00:23:17,813 --> 00:23:19,648
Levi Mercado, died.

542
00:23:19,731 --> 00:23:20,649
Isn't he Atoy's boss?

543
00:23:20,732 --> 00:23:21,566
Atoy's boss.

544
00:23:21,650 --> 00:23:22,400
[suspicious music playing]

545
00:23:22,484 --> 00:23:23,110
Let me see.

546
00:23:23,193 --> 00:23:25,695
[music continues]

547
00:23:25,779 --> 00:23:26,822
Who's behind this?

548
00:23:26,905 --> 00:23:29,366
[music swells]

549
00:23:31,451 --> 00:23:32,494
[music fades]

550
00:23:32,577 --> 00:23:33,745
Obsidian.

551
00:23:34,704 --> 00:23:36,414
Samir's terrorist group.

552
00:23:37,624 --> 00:23:39,000
He planned it all.

553
00:23:41,169 --> 00:23:43,171
He ambushed all our companions.

554
00:23:43,880 --> 00:23:46,216
Uno is in the ICU.

555
00:23:47,342 --> 00:23:50,679
[pensive music playing]

556
00:23:50,762 --> 00:23:51,805
Is that his way of getting back at you?

557
00:23:51,888 --> 00:23:54,182
[music continues]

558
00:23:54,266 --> 00:23:56,226
Why did he have to involve my colleagues?

559
00:23:56,726 --> 00:23:57,978
They were innocent.

560
00:23:59,521 --> 00:24:00,814
I really want to find him,

561
00:24:00,897 --> 00:24:02,315
I really want to kill him.

562
00:24:03,358 --> 00:24:06,361
But, Bro, what about
your promise to Audrey?

563
00:24:07,320 --> 00:24:09,114
Audrey doesn't need to know about this.

564
00:24:10,699 --> 00:24:11,449
Emerson…

565
00:24:12,993 --> 00:24:14,536
I have to do this.

566
00:24:15,620 --> 00:24:17,289
I can't go back to a normal life

567
00:24:17,372 --> 00:24:19,207
knowing I didn't do this.

568
00:24:19,791 --> 00:24:22,002
Bro, I'm scared for your family.

569
00:24:23,670 --> 00:24:25,422
And you're the only one left alive.

570
00:24:25,964 --> 00:24:27,674
They'll surely come looking for you.

571
00:24:28,300 --> 00:24:30,635
Then they should have done it earlier.

572
00:24:30,719 --> 00:24:34,472
[music continues]

573
00:24:34,556 --> 00:24:36,474
You know, Mercado was their target.

574
00:24:36,558 --> 00:24:38,476
[music continues]

575
00:24:38,560 --> 00:24:40,729
Mercado left me a note, he said…

576
00:24:41,730 --> 00:24:43,857
“Protect the Belladonna at all costs.”

577
00:24:43,940 --> 00:24:45,233
[music fades]

578
00:24:45,317 --> 00:24:46,860
Looks like that's the reason Samir

579
00:24:46,943 --> 00:24:47,861
came back here.

580
00:24:48,528 --> 00:24:52,532
[suspicious music playing]

581
00:24:52,616 --> 00:24:54,492
What could that be?

582
00:24:54,576 --> 00:24:55,452
What is it?

583
00:24:56,494 --> 00:24:57,787
Maybe it's…

584
00:24:58,496 --> 00:24:59,915
a code name?

585
00:24:59,998 --> 00:25:01,416
[music continues]

586
00:25:01,499 --> 00:25:03,251
Code name, maybe…

587
00:25:04,294 --> 00:25:05,545
Maybe a new…

588
00:25:05,629 --> 00:25:09,007
virus, or maybe a code for a…

589
00:25:09,090 --> 00:25:11,593
rocket ship or something.

590
00:25:11,676 --> 00:25:13,762
That's exactly what
I'll find out from Samir…

591
00:25:15,013 --> 00:25:16,973
before I kill him.

592
00:25:17,057 --> 00:25:20,518
[rousing music playing]

593
00:25:25,690 --> 00:25:29,069
[electronic blipping]

594
00:25:29,152 --> 00:25:34,616
tense music playing]

595
00:25:35,742 --> 00:25:36,493
Hi!

596
00:25:36,576 --> 00:25:38,328
You and your sister are transferees

597
00:25:38,411 --> 00:25:40,121
from a public school?

598
00:25:40,205 --> 00:25:42,165
Are you guys poor or something?

599
00:25:42,249 --> 00:25:42,999
Ibyang!

600
00:25:43,667 --> 00:25:45,710
Emerson, this is Jesabel.

601
00:25:45,794 --> 00:25:47,045
Jesabel, ah…

602
00:25:47,128 --> 00:25:48,046
Ah, my best friend, Emerson.

603
00:25:48,129 --> 00:25:49,673
Uncle Emerson!

604
00:25:49,756 --> 00:25:51,424
Yes, tracker in training.

605
00:25:51,508 --> 00:25:54,177
Where's the female patient

606
00:25:54,261 --> 00:25:56,096
from yesterday? The…

607
00:25:56,179 --> 00:25:58,014
the survivor from the Gregorio explosion.

608
00:25:58,098 --> 00:26:01,601
She was taken home by
the man who brought her here last night.

609
00:26:01,685 --> 00:26:03,812
I have doubts about that man.

610
00:26:03,895 --> 00:26:05,647
Ah, excuse me!

611
00:26:05,730 --> 00:26:07,065
Ah, Miss Japanese.

612
00:26:07,148 --> 00:26:08,024
[samurai swishes]

613
00:26:08,108 --> 00:26:10,652
[speaking in Japanese] Say
your prayers… this is your end!

614
00:26:10,735 --> 00:26:13,113
[samurai swishing & clanging]

615
00:26:13,697 --> 00:26:14,864
[grunting & groaning]

616
00:26:14,948 --> 00:26:16,199
[swishing & clanging]

617
00:26:16,283 --> 00:26:19,369
["Mamang Sastre" playing]

618
00:26:19,452 --> 00:26:21,496
Rachel C. Arias Script
Producer/Closed Caption Transcriptionist
